{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On Mount Sinai</b> — the section of the blasphemer is juxtaposed to <b>on Mount Sinai</b>, because at Sinai they heard the commandment and the whole world trembled, whereas this one heard and did not take heed. And further, as stated in Kiddushin there: a matter of four letters, sages hand it over to their students once a week. Therefore the section of Shemittah is juxtaposed to it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:28.156239355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}